 "_doc": "S6-B3139bh preparation (council B3139q-r41, \"the one thing first\"): the\nADMITTED institutional lines' exposure to the 13F look-ahead, read-only.\n\nTwo 13F producers feed the nine admitted institutional strategies, both\nmaking a holding usable at ReportPeriod + 45 days with no check that it was\nFILED (the per-ticker `Date` column is the SEC filing timestamp, verified\nS6-B3139ay):\n  1. smart_money.institutional_signal -> institutional_new_positions /\n     institutional_increased / institutional_buy (7 of the 9 gate on these).\n     Measured here per FIRE in the R5 merged cube: the stored value is\n     reproduced with the live function (control), then recomputed under the\n     FILED rule (available_after <= as_of AND Date <= as_of, bulk first then\n     per-ticker, the live precedence) and the strategy's own 13F gate\n     expression is re-evaluated. A fire whose 13F gate closes under the filed\n     rule is a trade that could not have been taken.\n  2. scripts/build_institutional_persistence_precompute.py -> yearly\n     snapshots feeding persistent_holders_4q / committed_growth_holders\n     (2 of the 9). Rebuilding a snapshot under the filed rule is ~1 h per\n     snapshot (the builder's own estimate), so this script measures the\n     INPUT exposure only: of the 13F rows each snapshot consumed, how many\n     carry Date > snapshot date (not yet public). That is an upper bound on\n     the rows that could move those two strategies' snapshot values.\n\nWrites output_audit/b3139bh_admitted_13f_exposure.json. Nothing in the\nengine, the roster or the admissions is touched.",
 "generated_batch": "B3139q-r42",
